  "description": "Debate rages over the correct way to make a classic Roman amatriciana sauce. Ours packs a delicate heat, sharp Pecorino Romano cheese, sweet-tart tomato sauce, and rich cured pork.",
  "notes": "Notes: Guanciale (cured pork jowl) will give the sauce the best texture, but if your best option is good pancetta, use it instead.\nBucatini is a type of thick, hollow spaghetti; you can substitute regular spaghetti, or even penne.",
